    ('p', 'A couture house rarely makes most of its money from couture. Couture is the top of the brand: the place where its ideas and craft are proven. Understanding this structure helps any designer plan a label that can grow.'),
    ('h2', '1. Signature codes'),
    ('p', 'Strong houses are recognisable without a logo: a silhouette, a colour, a motif or a technique that returns every season. For an Indian couturier this might be a signature embroidery, a heritage textile or a particular palette. Codes make the brand memorable and protect it from copies.'),
    ('h2', '2. The atelier story'),
